  {
    "episode_id": 51967,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51967.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "I'm Sarah Fensky. This morning, Congresswoman Cory Bush introduced a new bill. The topic is an area of particular interest for her and was long before she came to Washington. The People's Response Act aims to transform criminal justice in the U.S. by creating a new public safety agency. It would answer to the Department of Health and Human Services, not the Department of Justice. Congresswoman Bush joined us this morning to tell us all about it. Congresswoman Cory Bush, welcome. Thank you for having me. So in your bill, you see a new public safety agency. How would this new agency work?",
