        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Law enforcement agencies view increased use of social workers as a threat to their role and resources.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Federal action on social worker deployment could be perceived as undermining the existing justice system.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Public perception of 'defunding' is influenced by framing around resource allocation shifts toward non-police services.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Political resistance at the federal level is likely if the proposal is seen as weakening the Justice Department.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that concerns about backlash are relevant and should be addressed proactively.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 51967,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51967.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think this is the thing. Do we fund, would you go to a place to have services where the people aren't as well equipped to do something? I think about every time someone would come into a hospital and they would notice that a nurse was kind of new. And so they would say, I don't want that nurse. I want the nurse to give me this person over here because they wanted the one that has the skills that they felt more comfortable with because they wanted to make sure that they were taken care of in the best manner. So in the same way, why would we continue to fund an area that is not making sure that they're doing the best work? you know in that area when we have people who are trained and and and property that's not like saying that we should we should find our catering services we shouldn't find catering services to do police work and it would be hurtful to take that from them because like that doesn't make sense have the people who are killed and trained to do this isn't a not at law enforcement either this is to say you do you have a job but social work is also have a job",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
